   "updated": 1790826922400,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "step      theory                        what it tells you\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nFrame     Schön 1983, reflection-in-    frame, make a move, read what the\n          action                        result says back\n          Dorst & Cross 2001, co-       problem and solution change\n          evolution                     together\nGenerate  Hatchuel & Weil 2003, C-K     a concept cannot be decided with\n          theory                        today's knowledge; designing grows\n                                        both concepts and knowledge\n          Zwicky 1969, morphological    split into variables, combine the\n          analysis                      options of each\nStructure Suh 1990, axiomatic design    one parameter per requirement:\n                                        change one variable at a time\nPredict   Gero 1990, function-          compare the behaviour you expect\n          behaviour-structure           with what the structure will do\nChoose    Simon 1969, satisficing       good enough within constraints\n          Sobek, Ward & Liker 1999,     keep several options alive until\n          set-based design              a test decides\nProcess   Design Council 2005, Double   widen, then narrow, twice:\n          Diamond                       the problem, then the solution\n          Rittel & Webber 1973, wicked  no final formulation; every\n          problems                      release is itself a test",
   "originalText": "step      theory                        what it tells you\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nFrame     Schön 1983, reflection-in-    frame, make a move, read what the\n          action                        result says back\n          Dorst & Cross 2001, co-       problem and solution change\n          evolution                     together\nGenerate  Hatchuel & Weil 2003, C-K     a concept cannot be decided with\n          theory                        today's knowledge; designing grows\n                                        both concepts and knowledge\n          Zwicky 1969, morphological    split into variables, combine the\n          analysis                      options of each\nStructure Suh 1990, axiomatic design    one parameter per requirement:\n                                        change one variable at a time\nPredict   Gero 1990, function-          compare the behaviour you expect\n          behaviour-structure           with what the structure will do\nChoose    Simon 1969, satisficing       good enough within constraints\n          Sobek, Ward & Liker 1999,     keep several options alive until\n          set-based design              a test decides\nProcess   Design Council 2005, Double   widen, then narrow, twice:\n          Diamond                       the problem, then the solution\n          Rittel & Webber 1973, wicked  no final formulation; every\n          problems                      release is itself a test",
   "fontSize": 14,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "autoResize": true,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "why-foot",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 3370.0,
   "y": 1612,
   "width": 591.36,
   "height": 40.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1864ab",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": "frame-dt",
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 556540420,
   "version": 1,
