   "seed": 855964740,
   "version": 3,
   "versionNonce": 7115744,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1790857063029,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "1 · The design problem: abduction\n   only the value is known; frame a principle, then make options\n   Dorst 2011 · Simon 1969, satisficing\n\n2 · Inputs, process, output\n   in: aim · constraints · resources\n   do: frame · generate · predict · check · choose · test\n   out: artifact · rationale · bet · test plan · knowledge ↺\n\n3 · The theory behind each step\n   Schön · Dorst & Cross · C-K · Zwicky · Suh · Gero\n   Simon · set-based design · Double Diamond · Rittel & Webber\n\n4 · What to attend to, and what not to\n   the value, the frame, the variables, the bet\n   not: choose only among what was tried before\n\n5 · How the Design Workbench follows the theory\n   aim = Design Tasks · frame = Rationale · predict = Expectation\n   generate and check = Runs · choose = page Delivery",
   "originalText": "1 · The design problem: abduction\n   only the value is known; frame a principle, then make options\n   Dorst 2011 · Simon 1969, satisficing\n\n2 · Inputs, process, output\n   in: aim · constraints · resources\n   do: frame · generate · predict · check · choose · test\n   out: artifact · rationale · bet · test plan · knowledge ↺\n\n3 · The theory behind each step\n   Schön · Dorst & Cross · C-K · Zwicky · Suh · Gero\n   Simon · set-based design · Double Diamond · Rittel & Webber\n\n4 · What to attend to, and what not to\n   the value, the frame, the variables, the bet\n   not: choose only among what was tried before\n\n5 · How the Design Workbench follows the theory\n   aim = Design Tasks · frame = Rationale · predict = Expectation\n   generate and check = Runs · choose = page Delivery",
   "fontSize": 14,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "autoResize": true,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
